And also what it was like to write a show you had total control over the destiny of five characters when we can feel so out of control when it comes to our own.
还有，当我们在自己的命运方面感到如此失控时，写一部完全控制五个角色命运的剧是什么感觉？

01:07:33.587 --> 01:07:35.488
It's such a smart question.
这是一个非常聪明的问题。

01:07:35.488 --> 01:07:40.699
We wrote this pilot, again, not really knowing if it would go beyond this.
我们再次编写了这个试播集，但并不真正知道它是否会超出这个范围。

01:07:40.699 --> 01:07:44.432
And so we felt very much in the moment of that night.
所以那天晚上的那一刻我们感触良多。

01:07:44.432 --> 01:07:47.319
We had ideas for where the show would go.
我们对演出的走向有想法。

01:07:47.319 --> 01:07:55.206
But I never, even when we dove into really making it and having more and more ideas about how this would unfold.
但我从来没有这样做过，即使我们真正投入制作它并对如何展开有越来越多的想法。

01:07:55.206 --> 01:07:59.009
I never felt like masters of these characters destiny.
我从来没有觉得自己是这些角色命运的主人。

01:07:59.009 --> 01:08:03.516
I think Carter and I wanted to let these characters surprise us.
我想卡特和我想让这些角色给我们带来惊喜。

01:08:03.516 --> 01:08:06.192
We wanted to respect these characters.
我们想尊重这些角色。

01:08:06.192 --> 01:08:10.839
I came to have this delusional feeling like they were real people.
我开始有一种错觉，感觉他们是真人。

01:08:10.840 --> 01:08:14.840
I really like, I hear writers talk about that and I don't always feel that way when I write stuff.
我真的很喜欢，我听到作家们谈论这一点，但当我写东西时我并不总是有这种感觉。

01:08:15.480 --> 01:08:19.249
This was like by the end of how much your mother, these were real human beings to me.
这就像你的母亲对我来说是真正的人一样。

01:08:19.249 --> 01:08:20.935
I didn't feel like some puppet master.
我不觉得自己像个木偶大师。

01:08:20.935 --> 01:08:22.930
I felt like, I don't think Carter did either.
我觉得，我认为卡特也没有这么做。

01:08:22.930 --> 01:08:26.922
I think we felt like, These are our friends and we're kind of seeing what happens to them.
我想我们的感觉是，这些是我们的朋友，我们正在看看他们会发生什么。

01:08:26.922 --> 01:08:28.119
We're kind of guiding them.
我们有点引导他们。

01:08:28.920 --> 01:08:33.800
Every now and again, we'd feel like, okay, we have to make something bad happen to one of them.
时不时地，我们会觉得，好吧，我们必须让其中一个人发生一些不好的事情。

01:08:33.800 --> 01:08:35.623
We need, we need an emotional term.
我们需要，我们需要一个情感术语。

01:08:35.623 --> 01:08:38.279
We need to explore something hard and it felt evil.
我们需要探索一些艰难的事情，这感觉很邪恶。

01:08:39.000 --> 01:08:39.789
It felt evil.
感觉很邪恶。

01:08:39.789 --> 01:08:43.129
That's part of what I get from Jordan and his question.
这是我从乔丹和他的问题中得到的部分信息。

01:08:43.129 --> 01:08:49.444
We were controlling this destiny and we'd have to put them to this torture sometimes and especially Ted.
我们控制着这个命运，有时我们不得不让他们遭受这种折磨，尤其是特德。

01:08:49.444 --> 01:09:07.479
And we'd have to make our dear friend Josh Radner go into this kind of pain and do things like saying, blurting out I love you to Kobe Smolders and her in her apartment in the pilot and make them crawl through hard shit so we could come out the other side and all kind of learn something together.
我们必须让我们亲爱的朋友乔什·拉德纳（Josh Radner）陷入这种痛苦，做一些事情，比如在试播集中的科比·斯莫尔德斯（Kobe Smolders）和她的公寓里脱口而出我爱你，让他们在艰难的环境中爬行，这样我们才能从另一边走出来，一起学习一些东西。

01:09:07.479 --> 01:09:15.921
And often it was us making Carter myself, the other writers, stuff we took from Josh's life, other conversations we had with the actors.
通常是我们自己制作卡特，其他编剧，我们从乔什的生活中汲取的东西，以及我们与演员进行的其他对话。

01:09:15.921 --> 01:09:21.880
Like we would take our own really hard shit And put the characters through some version of that.
就像我们会采取我们自己的非常艰难的方式，然后让角色经历某种版本的情况。

01:09:21.880 --> 01:09:23.245
And so it felt shared.
所以感觉是共享的。

01:09:23.245 --> 01:09:25.479
We tried to feel the pain with them.
我们试着和他们一起感受痛苦。

01:09:27.079 --> 01:09:32.680
But was it strange to sort of come to feel like these were my friends almost like my family or my kids or something.
但感觉这些是我的朋友，几乎就像我的家人或我的孩子什么的，是不是有点奇怪。

01:09:33.159 --> 01:09:34.955
And then sometimes put them through hell.
然后有时会让他们经历地狱。

01:09:34.955 --> 01:09:39.159
But have this feeling like we're we all we knew it was all going to work out somehow in the end.
但要有这种感觉，就像我们都知道这一切最终都会以某种方式解决。

01:09:39.319 --> 01:09:41.516
But even the end was complicated, right?
但即使是结局也很复杂，对吧？

01:09:41.516 --> 01:09:47.720
And there is there a neat bow on any chapter of life ever really quite just sort of keeps going and complicating.
人生的任何一章都有一个简洁的蝴蝶结，真的只是不断地前进和复杂化。

01:09:47.720 --> 01:09:51.760
and that sort of Ted's lesson in the pilot and in the series.
以及特德在试播集和剧集中的教训。

01:09:51.760 --> 01:09:58.920
And so I guess I felt a great deal of respect and a great deep, almost delusional connection to these characters as we wrote them.
所以我想当我们写这些角色时，我对这些角色感到了极大的尊重和一种深刻的、近乎妄想的联系。

01:09:58.920 --> 01:10:09.000
And I felt like I was going through it with them and sort of cathartically putting some of my own shit or Carter's shit or whatever into these characters' lives and seeing what happened to them.
我觉得我正在和他们一起经历这一切，并以一种宣泄的方式将我自己的一些狗屎或卡特的狗屎或其他什么东西放入这些角色的生活中，看看他们发生了什么。

01:10:09.000 --> 01:10:10.920
But it was always with great care.
但总是非常小心。

01:10:10.920 --> 01:10:12.119
Some of them as I felt very guilty.
他们中的一些人让我感到非常内疚。

01:10:12.119 --> 01:10:20.319
I felt guilty making Ted go like, what do you use that conversation you cited, Josh, where you're like, can't Ted just have a good moment and not be kicked in the nuts of the next episode.
让泰德这样说，我感到内疚，你用你引用的那段对话做什么，乔什，你就像，泰德不能只是享受美好时光，而不会在下一集里被踢疯。

01:10:20.319 --> 01:10:22.720
It's an interesting thing.
这是一件有趣的事情。

01:10:22.720 --> 01:10:28.359
It becomes a seduatiatorial Roman Gladiator, like let's throw some lions in there and see what happens.
它变成了一个具有镇静作用的罗马角斗士，就像我们把一些狮子扔进去，看看会发生什么。

01:10:28.359 --> 01:10:36.680
Did you and Carter talk so more globally about the idea of Destiny as a major theme of the show?
您和卡特是否在全球范围内广泛谈论过将命运作为该剧的主题的想法？

01:10:36.680 --> 01:10:46.520
Yeah, I mean, we definitely, but also I think Destiny as defined in how much mother to me is sort of the sense you make of things later.
是的，我的意思是，我们当然，但我也认为命运的定义是对我来说有多少母亲是你后来对事物的理解。

01:10:46.520 --> 01:10:54.880
I think in 2030, future Ted can see a sense of destiny and can see, or magic, whatever you want to call it.
我认为到 2030 年，未来的泰德可以看到一种命运感，可以看到，或者魔法，无论你怎么称呼它。

01:10:54.880 --> 01:10:55.800
Or order.
或者订购。

01:10:55.800 --> 01:10:59.720
Destiny sounds almost too neat for a lot of what happened on that show.
对于这部剧中发生的很多事情来说，命运听起来太完美了。

01:10:59.720 --> 01:11:09.720
I mean, Destiny puts you in certain right places, at certain right times, and then life gets complicated in some whole other way after that wonderful moment.
我的意思是，命运把你放在某些正确的地方，在某些正确的时间，然后在那美妙的时刻之后，生活会以完全不同的方式变得复杂。

01:11:09.720 --> 01:11:22.560
I always love that, that Kierkegaard quote that I think is really, I sound like Ted right now, but it's a really, it's so appropriate for how I met my mother that life can only be understood backward, but you have to live it forward.
我一直很喜欢克尔凯郭尔的那句话，我觉得这句话真的，我现在听起来就像特德，但这真的非常适合我如何认识我的母亲，生活只能向后理解，但你必须向前生活。

01:11:22.560 --> 01:11:24.119
Yeah, and yeah, that's the show.
是啊，是啊，这就是节目。

01:11:24.119 --> 01:11:25.640
So you get both of them in there.
所以你把他们两个都放在那里。

01:11:25.640 --> 01:11:27.680
Which we quoted that in the pitch.
我们在演讲中引用了这一点。

01:11:27.680 --> 01:11:32.680
You get older Ted who knows where all this is headed.
随着年龄的增长，泰德知道这一切的走向。

01:11:32.960 --> 01:11:37.359
He knows all the twists and turns and he knows how he landed on his feet.
他知道所有的曲折，也知道他是如何站稳脚跟的。

01:11:37.359 --> 01:11:40.840
And then the Ted that I was playing doesn't know any of that.
然后我扮演的 Ted 对此一无所知。

01:11:40.840 --> 01:11:47.520
The Ted that I was playing was like, This is the worst night of my life, or this is calamitous, this is never, I'm done, I'm not gonna be successful.
我扮演的泰德就像是，这是我一生中最糟糕的夜晚，或者这是灾难性的，这永远不会，我受够了，我不会成功。

01:11:47.520 --> 01:11:51.319
I'm not gonna have a family, like all of these things.
我不会有一个家庭，就像所有这些事情一样。

01:11:51.319 --> 01:11:59.680
I sometimes, I used to think about like if you, this is a weird thought experiment, but it pertains to the show.
有时我会想，如果你的话，这是一个奇怪的思想实验，但它与节目有关。

01:11:59.680 --> 01:12:08.640
If you were a molecule in a cell and you were like sentient, like you could, you knew you were a molecule in a cell and you could be interviewed.
如果你是细胞中的一个分子，并且你就像有感知能力一样，你就知道你是细胞中的一个分子，你可以接受采访。

01:12:08.640 --> 01:12:11.520
And so I said, what's it like being a molecule in this cell?
所以我说，作为这个细胞中的一个分子是什么样的？

01:12:11.520 --> 01:12:13.399
You'd be like, it's insane, man.
你会说，这太疯狂了，伙计。

01:12:13.399 --> 01:12:15.039
I'm getting knocked around.
我快被打晕了。

01:12:15.039 --> 01:12:17.119
Like, I don't know what's going on.
就像，我不知道发生了什么事。

01:12:17.119 --> 01:12:19.199
It's just anarchy in here.
这里只是无政府状态。

01:12:19.199 --> 01:12:28.840
But the scientist looking through a microscope sees that there's a real order to what's going on in that cell and that molecule has a destiny of some sort.
但通过显微镜观察的科学家发现，细胞中发生的事情确实有顺序，并且该分子具有某种命运。

01:12:28.840 --> 01:12:30.600
Like, it's going to, right?
就像，它会的，对吧？

01:12:30.600 --> 01:12:34.479
But from the perspective of the molecule, it doesn't know that.
但从分子的角度来看，它并不知道这一点。

01:12:34.479 --> 01:12:40.960
And I always thought that was kind of like how I made my mother like, Ted was the molecule getting knocked around inside the cell.
我一直认为这有点像我让我母亲喜欢的方式，特德是细胞内被撞击的分子。

01:12:40.960 --> 01:12:50.279
But then the older Ted was kind of the scientist who was like, no, no, no, I see how this is all coalescing and gathering steam and making sense.
但年长的特德就像一位科学家，他说，不，不，不，我看到这一切是如何融合在一起、聚集在一起并有意义的。

01:12:50.279 --> 01:12:50.840
You know?
你知道？

01:12:50.840 --> 01:13:07.680
Yeah, and I think like Destiny in the world of the show to me is like the gratitude you feel for your life looking back and realizing that even the hard parts had to happen and they made you who you are and you survived them and you became who you are now and you're happy to be.
是的，我认为这部剧世界中的《命运》对我来说就像是你对自己的生活的感激之情，当你回顾自己的生活时，意识到即使是困难的部分也必须发生，它们造就了你，你熬过了它们，你成为了现在的你，你很高兴成为这样的人。

01:13:07.680 --> 01:13:12.560
And you only achieve Destiny when you're content to where you are and you're accepting where you are.
只有当你对自己所处的位置感到满意并接受自己的位置时，你才能实现命运。

01:13:12.560 --> 01:13:14.539
And when you're young, it's hard to feel that.
当你年轻的时候，很难有这种感觉。

01:13:14.539 --> 01:13:31.239
Yeah, and also I think because we live in such a kind of insanely upbeat and optimistic culture where we're shadowed denying and death denying and pain and suffering denying, if you really ask people, what were the most meaningful moments of your life?
是的，而且我认为，因为我们生活在一种极其乐观的文化中，我们被否认、否认死亡、否认痛苦和苦难所笼罩，如果你真的问人们，你一生中最有意义的时刻是什么？

01:13:31.239 --> 01:13:36.520
They often involve struggle and heartbreak and set back an unexpected turn of events, right?
它们常常涉及斗争和心碎，并让事情发生意想不到的转变，对吗？

01:13:36.520 --> 01:13:41.800
They're never like a graduate from business school I met the girl in my dreams and I had no problem.
他们从来都不像商学院的毕业生，我在梦中遇到了那个女孩，我没有遇到任何问题。

01:13:41.800 --> 01:13:49.159
That's not what Forge is character, both in the larger sense of the word character and in this specific sense, Forge is these characters.
这并不是 Forge 所代表的角色，无论是在角色这个词的更广泛意义上，还是在这个特定的意义上，Forge 就是这些角色。

01:13:49.159 --> 01:14:07.800
So I think that dual kind of consciousness of watching people live forward not knowing how this is going to unfold and being quite scared but doing the best they could and then the older perspective of almost like he's watching himself and saying, keep going, kid.
所以我认为，这种双重意识是看着人们向前生活，不知道事情会如何发展，非常害怕，但会尽力而为，然后从旧的角度看，就像他在看着自己说，继续前进，孩子。

01:14:07.800 --> 01:14:16.121
it's going to, you know, almost like me talking to myself, when I watched the pilot, like, hey, hey, you were, you did okay.
你知道，这几乎就像我自言自语，当我观看飞行员时，就像，嘿，嘿，你是，你做得很好。

01:14:16.121 --> 01:14:16.993
You did okay.
你做得很好。

01:14:16.993 --> 01:14:18.604
You landed on your feet.
你双脚着地。

01:14:18.604 --> 01:14:24.577
So, Craig, did we officially or did you officially rename the pilot the blue french horn?
那么，克雷格，我们正式还是您正式将飞行员重新命名为蓝色圆号？

01:14:24.577 --> 01:14:25.785
In my mind, I did.
在我看来，我做到了。

01:14:25.785 --> 01:14:26.657
How did I go?
我怎么去的？

01:14:26.657 --> 01:14:29.610
Is there a time machine so I can go do that?
有时光机让我可以去那儿吗？

01:14:29.610 --> 01:14:31.757
It should have been called that.
应该这么称呼。

01:14:31.757 --> 01:14:33.032
I can admit it now.
我现在可以承认了。

01:14:33.032 --> 01:14:44.240
The one to punch a blue french horn and purple giraffe would I mean, you might have colors, it's all colors, you might have wanted every episode to have a color in it.
我的意思是，打蓝色法国号和紫色长颈鹿的那个，你可能有颜色，都是颜色，你可能希望每一集都有一种颜色。

01:14:44.239 --> 01:14:45.270
That damn it.
真该死。

01:14:45.270 --> 01:14:52.670
Every fucking pilot's called pilot and we should just need that to be retcon, I don't know what to do about it.
每个该死的飞行员都被称为飞行员，我们只需要进行侦察即可，我不知道该怎么办。

01:14:52.670 --> 01:14:53.670
All right, I'll talk to the studio.
好的，我去跟工作室谈谈。

01:14:53.670 --> 01:14:55.149
They made that time machine.
他们制造了那台时光机。

01:14:55.149 --> 01:15:03.189
Well, before recording this episode, we asked you on Instagram from at how we made your mother.
好吧，在录制本集之前，我们在 Instagram 上询问了您的问题：我们是如何创造您的母亲的。

01:15:03.189 --> 01:15:08.170
If you had any questions about the pilot, by the time we had finished recording, an hour later.
如果您对试播集有任何疑问，当我们在一小时后完成录制时。

01:15:08.170 --> 01:15:09.377
over 300 questions.
超过 300 个问题。

01:15:09.377 --> 01:15:12.173
So thank you for sending those questions in.
感谢您发送这些问题。

01:15:12.173 --> 01:15:25.580
So we can announce now that you can look forward to bonus episodes that we are calling general questions, general questions, general questions, where we rapid fire go through as many of your questions as we can.
因此，我们现在可以宣布，您可以期待我们称之为一般问题、一般问题、一般问题的奖励剧集，我们将尽可能多地快速解答您的问题。

01:15:25.580 --> 01:15:27.486
We'll be doing that each week.
我们每周都会这样做。

01:15:27.486 --> 01:15:32.569
So just look out on Instagram for posting, asking you to submit those questions.
因此，请留意 Instagram 上的帖子，要求您提交这些问题。

01:15:32.569 --> 01:15:36.345
but also on the website, we're collecting your stories.
我们还在网站上收集您的故事。

01:15:36.345 --> 01:15:42.730
These are stories of how you discovered, how I met your mother, hard times I got you through.
这些故事讲述了你如何发现，我如何遇见你母亲，以及我如何帮助你度过难关。

01:15:42.730 --> 01:15:46.232
Generally, what how I met your mother means to you.
一般来说，我如何认识你母亲对你来说意味着什么。

01:15:46.232 --> 01:15:51.449
So go to www.howwemadeyourmother.com, click on contact to submit your story.
因此，请访问 www.howwemadeyourmother.com，点击“联系方式”提交您的故事。

