And here is an amazing one.
这是一个令人惊奇的事情。

01:15:54.037 --> 01:15:56.388
This is from Nephthes, from Paris.
这是来自巴黎的 Nephthes。

01:15:56.388 --> 01:16:00.260
Oh, this is like the greatest thing We've ever had this.
哦，这就像我们经历过的最伟大的事情。

01:16:00.260 --> 01:16:04.201
This is the one we cheated and we read ahead on this one.
这是我们作弊的，我们提前阅读了这一点。

01:16:04.201 --> 01:16:08.212
Yeah, this is yeah, this is quite an Extraordinary letter.
是的，这是是的，这是一封非常特别的信。

01:16:08.212 --> 01:16:13.675
So we are so grateful for you Nefty's from I hope I'm pronouncing it correctly.
所以我们非常感谢你 Nefty's from 我希望我的发音正确。

01:16:13.675 --> 01:16:14.175
I know.
我知道。

01:16:14.175 --> 01:16:15.903
I don't know what to say.
我不知道该说什么。

01:16:15.903 --> 01:16:28.073
Nefty's from Paris sending this in salute I was 12 years old the first time I stumbled upon how I met your mother it was 2013 I was with my brother's girlfriends little sister.
来自巴黎的 Nefty 向您致以敬意 我 12 岁时第一次偶然发现我是如何遇见你母亲的，那是 2013 年，当时我和我哥哥的女朋友的小妹妹在一起。

01:16:28.073 --> 01:16:29.940
We were very close friends.
我们是非常亲密的朋友。

01:16:29.940 --> 01:16:36.025
We had no money me and spent our time inventing games, lives, and careers for ourselves.
我们没有钱，把时间花在为自己发明游戏、生活和职业上。

01:16:36.010 --> 01:16:46.369
She had a tiny purple couch with green stripes, and sometimes we could watch series and movies on a tiny cathode-ray TV that her mother had found at a flea market, if I remember correctly.
她有一张带有绿色条纹的紫色小沙发，如果我没记错的话，有时我们可以在她母亲在跳蚤市场找到的一台小型阴极射线电视上观看连续剧和电影。

01:16:46.369 --> 01:16:49.970
That's where we discovered our love for sitcoms, especially how I met your mother.
这就是我们发现自己对情景喜剧的热爱的地方，尤其是我是如何认识你母亲的。

01:16:49.970 --> 01:16:51.289
I love how the scene is set.
我喜欢场景的设置。

01:16:51.289 --> 01:16:52.770
I love the description of the couch.
我喜欢对沙发的描述。

01:16:52.770 --> 01:16:54.569
I'm already in.
我已经进去了

01:16:54.569 --> 01:16:57.529
This series has been with me for so many years.
这个系列已经陪伴我很多年了。

01:16:57.529 --> 01:17:03.000
I watch it when I'm happy, when I'm sad, when I'm sick, and when I'm perfectly fine.
当我快乐的时候、当我悲伤的时候、当我生病的时候、当我完全好的时候，我都会看它。

01:17:03.000 --> 01:17:06.340
I didn't grow up in a functional, happy, or loving family.
我并不是在一个正常的、幸福的、充满爱的家庭中长大的。

01:17:06.340 --> 01:17:10.140
How I met your mother taught me that this wasn't a life sentence.
我认识你母亲的经历告诉我这不是无期徒刑。

01:17:10.140 --> 01:17:13.300
That home is wherever you choose to make it.
那个家就是你选择的地方。

01:17:13.300 --> 01:17:18.100
My home wasn't a place of shouting in tears, even if that's where I was born.
我的家不是一个哭泣的地方，即使那是我出生的地方。

01:17:18.100 --> 01:17:24.420
My home can be anywhere with anyone, and I build it every day with that thought in my heart.
我的家可以在任何地方，与任何人在一起，我每天都怀着这样的想法建造它。

01:17:24.420 --> 01:17:29.680
This show taught me not to give up and to cherish what brings joy in life.
这个节目教会了我不要放弃并珍惜生活中带来的快乐。

01:17:29.680 --> 01:17:42.420
Today I'm 23 years old, I live in Paris, and I'm a young journalist who meets her friends several times a week at the same bars, tells the same stories on repeat, makes the same jokes and talks about love with her group in every conversation.
今天，我 23 岁了，我住在巴黎，我是一名年轻的记者，每周在同一家酒吧与她的朋友见面几次，重复讲述相同的故事，讲相同的笑话，并在每次谈话中与她的团队谈论爱。

01:17:42.420 --> 01:17:46.920
When I'm surrounded by this family I chose, sometimes often, I think of you.
当我被这个我选择的家庭包围时，有时我会经常想起你。

01:17:46.920 --> 01:17:54.770
I tell myself that without this show, I might never have managed to escape the toxic environment I grew up in.
我告诉自己，如果没有这个节目，我可能永远无法摆脱我成长的有毒环境。

01:17:54.770 --> 01:17:58.464
I once shared my love for how I met your mother the dear friend.
我曾经分享过我对如何认识你母亲这位亲爱的朋友的爱。

01:17:58.464 --> 01:18:11.397
Our teenage days were filled with references, singing bang, bang, bang, adi bang at the top of our lungs, throwing slap bets left and right, granting each other favors without question and using weight for it in every sense.
我们的青少年时代充满了参考资料，用尽全力唱着“砰、砰、砰、阿迪砰”，左右打赌，毫无疑问地互相给予对方好处，并在各种意义上使用重量。

01:18:11.397 --> 01:18:19.825
That friendship changed my life so intense, so complicated that even though it ended long ago, I will always think of her whenever I think of you.
那段友谊如此强烈、如此复杂地改变了我的生活，即使它早已结束，但每当我想起你时，我总会想起她。

01:18:19.825 --> 01:18:26.465
One night we slept over at each other's place and in the morning, she left an unexpected gift, an unspoken message.
一天晚上，我们在彼此的住处过夜，早上，她留下了一份意想不到的礼物，一条无言的信息。

01:18:26.465 --> 01:18:29.813
She placed a pineapple on my nightstand, and I understood.
她在我的床头柜上放了一个菠萝，我明白了。

01:18:29.813 --> 01:18:34.432
My first love gave me a blue French horn necklace for our first Valentine's Day.
我的初恋情人在我们的第一个情人节送给了我一条蓝色法国号项链。

01:18:34.432 --> 01:18:37.954
I made him watch every season any cried for hours at the end.
我让他看每一季，最后都会哭上几个小时。

01:18:37.954 --> 01:18:43.149
I have forced dozens of people to watch this series and I've never left anyone unaffected.
我已经强迫几十个人观看这个系列节目，而且我从来没有让任何人不受影响。

01:18:43.149 --> 01:18:45.702
Because that's how I met your mother represents to me.
因为这就是我认识你母亲的方式。

01:18:45.702 --> 01:18:53.029
Every person who has known me has heard me talk about this show, and every person who no longer knows me will think of me when whenever they hear its name.
每个认识我的人都听过我谈论过这个节目，每个不认识我的人一听到它的名字就会想起我。

01:18:53.029 --> 01:18:58.350
I grew up with you at McLaren's and I will never stop being grateful for what you have given me.
我和您一起在迈凯伦车队长大，我将永远感激您所给予我的一切。

01:18:58.350 --> 01:19:02.189
Thank you, Marshall, for teaching me that kindness is the key to all relationships.
谢谢你，马歇尔，你教会我善良是所有关系的关键。

01:19:02.189 --> 01:19:08.470
Thank you, Lily, for teaching me to be a loyal friend, always there for my loved ones without losing myself in the process.
谢谢你，莉莉，教会我成为一个忠诚的朋友，永远陪伴在我所爱的人身边，同时又不会在这个过程中迷失自我。

01:19:08.470 --> 01:19:13.430
Thank you, Robin, for teaching me that in the end, you have to be able to rely on yourself.
谢谢你，罗宾，你教会了我，最终你必须能够依靠自己。

01:19:13.430 --> 01:19:17.109
Thank you, Barney, for reminding me how important it is to have fun.
谢谢你，巴尼，提醒我玩得开心是多么重要。

01:19:17.109 --> 01:19:22.720
Thank you, Ted, for showing me that everything should be done with love, never out of fear.
谢谢你，特德，让我知道一切都应该用爱来完成，而不是出于恐惧。

01:19:22.720 --> 01:19:24.640
Thank you all for everything.
谢谢大家所做的一切。

01:19:24.640 --> 01:19:28.760
You have been with me for two thirds of my life and this journey will likely never end.
你陪伴了我三分之二的人生，这段旅程可能永远不会结束。

01:19:28.760 --> 01:19:31.479
I could write for hours more, but it's already late.
我可以再写几个小时，但已经晚了。

01:19:31.479 --> 01:19:35.920
And as we all know, nothing good ever happens after two AM.
众所周知，凌晨两点之后就不会发生任何好事。

01:19:35.920 --> 01:19:38.229
Thank you.
谢谢。

01:19:38.229 --> 01:19:39.590
Wow.
哇。

01:19:39.590 --> 01:19:44.529
I got choked up the first time I read that and I got choked up listening to it just now.
我第一次读到这个的时候就哽咽了，现在再听也哽咽了。

01:19:44.529 --> 01:19:46.090
Beautiful, beautiful.
美丽，美丽。

01:19:46.090 --> 01:19:48.289
That is why we made the show.
这就是我们制作这个节目的原因。

01:19:48.289 --> 01:19:51.569
Thank you for that beautiful message.
谢谢你的美丽留言。

01:19:51.569 --> 01:19:54.409
Really, really moved hearing that, really moved.
听了真的很感动，真的很感动。

01:19:54.409 --> 01:20:16.000
Yeah, I've read it a few times and I'm stunned at the sincerity and the, you know, I think back of like movies and TV, like sometimes it's filled with toxic silly nonsense.
是的，我读过几次，我对它的诚意感到震惊，你知道，我回想起电影和电视，有时它充满了有毒的愚蠢的废话。

01:20:16.000 --> 01:20:17.279
And some of this show was too.
这个节目的一些内容也是如此。

01:20:17.279 --> 01:20:19.359
And we're atoning for that.
我们正在为此赎罪。

01:20:19.359 --> 01:20:32.510
But a lot of, you know, I learned how, like, I mean, I learned how to, you know, talk to women or even talk to friends.
但很多，你知道，我学会了如何，我的意思是，我学会了如何，你知道，与女人交谈，甚至与朋友交谈。

01:20:32.510 --> 01:20:40.470
Like, there was so much that I learned from television and learned from, you know, when you fall in love with a TV series or fall in love with a movie.
就像，我从电视中学到了很多东西，你知道，当你爱上电视剧或爱上电影时，我学到了很多东西。

01:20:40.470 --> 01:20:41.909
I mean, it was so trippy for me.
我的意思是，这对我来说太迷幻了。

01:20:41.909 --> 01:20:45.710
Like, I was such a fan of that first karate kid movie.
就像，我是第一部空手道小子电影的粉丝。

01:20:45.710 --> 01:20:51.231
Like, to have Billy's abka and Ralph Nachio on the show like they're on my phone now.
就像，让比利的阿布卡和拉尔夫·纳奇奥出现在节目中，就像他们现在在我的手机上一样。

01:20:51.231 --> 01:20:53.180
Like I really like those guys.
就像我真的很喜欢那些家伙一样。

01:20:53.180 --> 01:20:54.350
They're fantastic.
他们太棒了。

01:20:54.350 --> 01:20:55.168
They're great.
他们很棒。

01:20:55.168 --> 01:20:57.622
Yeah, I mean, just the trippiness of that.
是的，我的意思是，这就是迷幻。

01:20:57.622 --> 01:21:08.551
But that move, I mean, talk about, I mean, Elizabeth Schoole, I was like my first crush or one of my first crushes like in that movie, I just remember how much I learned from film and TV.
但我的意思是，谈论这一举动，我的意思是，伊丽莎白·斯库勒，我就像我的第一次迷恋或我第一次迷恋的人，就像那部电影一样，我只记得我从电影和电视中学到了多少东西。

01:21:08.551 --> 01:21:11.064
And again, not all of it was great lessons.
再说一次，并非所有这些都是很好的教训。

01:21:11.064 --> 01:21:22.110
I had to unlearn some of those lessons, but it's so incredible to be a part of a show that takes up permanent residents within people's hearts and psyches and I'm just really stunned by it.
我不得不忘记其中的一些教训，但能够成为一部永久居民在人们内心和心灵中的节目的一部分真是太不可思议了，我真的对此感到震惊。

01:21:23.149 --> 01:21:24.028
It is stunning.
这是令人惊叹的。

01:21:24.028 --> 01:21:24.848
It's stunning.
太棒了。

01:21:24.848 --> 01:21:25.786
That's the word.
就是这个词。

01:21:25.786 --> 01:21:33.869
I feel stunned by it and to have a fan like that who really got what the show was and then brought it around to all of these other people.
我对此感到震惊，并拥有这样的粉丝，他们真正理解了这部剧的内涵，然后将其传播给所有其他人。

01:21:33.869 --> 01:21:35.379
I mean, that is the dream.
我的意思是，这就是梦想。

01:21:35.379 --> 01:21:36.308
To cool to show.
炫酷地展示。

01:21:36.308 --> 01:21:37.295
That's the dream.
这就是梦想。

01:21:37.295 --> 01:21:38.920
That's why we made the show.
这就是我们制作这个节目的原因。

01:21:38.920 --> 01:22:25.709
It was kind of a message in the bottle to find somebody exactly like this wonderful person who shared this message and part where they said it wasn't a life sentence to grow up in a hard place and a hard time and a hard home to grow up and then realize that it's not a life sentence that you can find a family and then sort of within this little letter of flashing forward to Paris in 23 years old and a young journalist who meets her friends several times a week at the bar and is kind of living her version of how much your mother, it's just so epic and scope the show kind of carried through that timeline of her life and just to think of it being an important part of that journey and getting and giving faith and hope and something to look forward to and realizing you're not stuck in a bad situation.
这是一种瓶子里的信息，找到一个与这个美妙的人一模一样的人分享了这个信息，他们说在一个艰难的地方、艰难的时光和艰难的家庭中长大并不是无期徒刑，然后意识到这不是无期徒刑，你可以找到一个家庭，然后在这封小信中，23岁的她突然来到了巴黎，一个年轻的记者每周在酒吧与她的朋友见面几次，生活在她的版本中，你的母亲有多少，这部剧的史诗般的规模和范围贯穿了她一生的时间线，只是想想它是这段旅程的重要组成部分，获得并给予信心和希望，以及一些值得期待的东西，并意识到你并没有陷入糟糕的境地。

01:22:25.709 --> 01:22:35.171
You can you can choose your way into better situations and you know the idea that the show inspired that is is really amazing thank you for sharing that That's it.
你可以选择进入更好的情况的方式，你知道这个节目所激发的想法真是太棒了，谢谢你分享，就是这样。

01:22:35.171 --> 01:22:36.681
It also strikes me, Craig.
这也让我印象深刻，克雷格。

01:22:36.681 --> 01:22:51.310
It's like, you know how there's that kind of, I mean, speaking of Star Wars, which you know a lot better than I do, but like that kind of charge where people say like fans understand the series better than George Lucas does at some like cellular level.
就像，你知道，我的意思是，谈到《星球大战》，你比我更了解它，但就像人们说的那样，粉丝比乔治·卢卡斯在细胞层面上更了解这个系列。

01:22:51.949 --> 01:23:04.002
Like, not that you and Carter don't understand this show, I just feel like at some point when a show permeates into the culture, it's actually belongs to the fans more than it belongs to the people who created it.
就像，并不是说你和卡特不理解这个节目，我只是觉得在某个时刻，当一个节目渗透到文化中时，它实际上更多地属于粉丝，而不是属于创造它的人。

01:23:04.002 --> 01:23:15.544
And the fans actually are going to have insight into things and make connections and draw like certain parallels that you didn't even see or themes that they can tease out that they've watched it so much.
粉丝们实际上会对事物有洞察力，建立联系，并画出某些你甚至没有看到的相似之处，或者他们可以梳理出他们已经看了很多次的主题。

01:23:15.544 --> 01:23:30.030
I mean genuinely when people come up to me and say I've seen the show 17 times like I have not seen all these episodes like they know this show way better than I know this show or they'll throw like an old joke at me and I'm like I don't know what that is.
我的意思是说，当人们来找我，说我已经看过这个节目 17 遍了，就像我没有看过所有这些剧集一样，他们比我更了解这个节目，或者他们会像一个老笑话一样对我扔，我就像我不知道那是什么。

01:23:30.029 --> 01:23:33.789
And they're like, they think I'm lying.
他们认为我在撒谎。

01:23:33.789 --> 01:23:36.630
Like they think that it's like part of my like DNA.
就像他们认为这是我 DNA 的一部分一样。

01:23:36.630 --> 01:23:38.590
That, you know, I don't like, I don't remember that.
你知道，我不喜欢，我不记得了。

01:23:38.590 --> 01:23:46.229
It was, it was, it was 2008, but it does feel like the fans own it.
那是，那是，那是2008年，但确实感觉球迷拥有它。

01:23:46.229 --> 01:23:54.270
It's theirs, you know, and in some ways we're going back and saying to the fans, hey, tell us what this thing is that we made.
这是他们的，你知道，在某些方面我们会回去对粉丝们说，嘿，告诉我们我们做了什么。

01:23:54.270 --> 01:23:55.270
Tell us what this is.
告诉我们这是什么。

01:23:55.270 --> 01:23:57.869
That is what, that's what this whole podcast is.
这就是整个播客的内容。

01:23:57.869 --> 01:24:02.989
I'm loving it so much because at the time I identified, I over-identified with it.
我非常喜欢它，因为当我认同它时，我过度认同它。

01:24:02.989 --> 01:24:04.069
I thought, this is me.
我想，这就是我。

01:24:04.069 --> 01:24:12.989
This is the, you know, I am only identified by this thing we're making in this moment in my 30s and this is my shot and this is every up and down.
你知道，这就是我在 30 多岁时唯一能通过我们正在制作的东西来识别的东西，这是我的镜头，这是每一次的起起落落。

01:24:12.989 --> 01:24:22.310
I'll take it all like it's me, I'll feel like I've failed if it's not great, et cetera, over, you know, the lows are always lower than the highs but you'll be, you identify entirely by it.
我会像我一样接受这一切，如果不是很好，我会觉得自己失败了，等等，结束了，你知道，低点总是低于高点，但你会，你完全通过它来识别。

01:24:22.310 --> 01:24:29.109
There's such freedom and just what a gift to realize It's so much bigger than any one person.
如此自由，意识到它比任何一个人都伟大得多，这真是一份礼物。

01:24:29.109 --> 01:24:36.189
It's not me, with the show finished 10, 11 years ago now, and it's finding people and it's becoming theirs.
不是我，这部剧已经在十、十一年前结束了，它正在寻找人们，它正在成为他们的。

01:24:36.189 --> 01:24:46.989
And to go back into it from outside now and experiencing it through the fans eyes and realizing what it meant to people, it's a humbling in the best possible way.
现在从外面回到这里，通过球迷的眼睛体验它，并意识到它对人们意味着什么，这是一种最好的谦卑。

01:24:46.989 --> 01:24:48.949
It makes me feel so small.
这让我感觉自己是如此的渺小。

01:24:48.949 --> 01:25:04.470
And like, it was our job just to channel this bigger thing, capture it in this moment of time where we're so lucky I'll be in the same place at the same time, picking up on the same radio of signal together from the universe and sort of channel it into this thing, send it out into the world and see what happens.
就像，我们的工作就是引导这个更大的东西，在这个时刻捕捉它，我们很幸运，我会在同一时间在同一个地方，从宇宙中一起接收同一个无线电信号，并将其引导到这个东西中，将其发送到世界上，看看会发生什么。

01:25:04.470 --> 01:25:06.310
And this is the part where we get to see what happened.
这是我们可以看到发生了什么的部分。

01:25:06.310 --> 01:25:07.750
And it's wonderful.
这太棒了。

01:25:07.750 --> 01:25:10.140
I am guilty.
我有罪。

01:25:10.140 --> 01:25:12.020
Please equip me.
请装备我。

01:25:12.020 --> 01:25:14.380
All sins are forgiven.
所有的罪孽都被宽恕了。

